# The pre-computed embedding cassette (ol-opmb.2 [TB-2]) — a local, derived
# artifact written by scripts/precompute-embeddings.mjs and copied into
# dist/ verbatim by build.mjs. Never committed: it is reproducible from
# olea-synthetic's retrieval-corpus.ts + queries.ts plus one priced,
# spend-guarded model pass, and re-generating it costs nothing once cached.
.embedding-cassette/

# The pre-computed generation cassette (ol-opmb.3 [TB-3]) — same reasoning as
# .embedding-cassette/ above, written by scripts/precompute-generation.mjs.
# NOTE: `.generation-cassette/*` (not a bare `.generation-cassette/`) is deliberate —
# a bare directory pattern stops git from even looking inside it, which defeats the
# negation exception right below (a classic gitignore footgun: negating a path inside
# an already-ignored DIRECTORY does nothing unless the directory pattern itself is a
# wildcard on contents, not the directory name).
.generation-cassette/*

# EXCEPTION: simulator-cassette.json (WBX-16e, ol-3ux7.64.18.5) does NOT fit the
# "reproducible, so never commit it" reasoning above — it is a small, hand-curated
# subset of one real staging recording (a judge verdict for the fixture explain-back
# journey's exact payload), and the model call it records is not deterministically
# reproducible by re-running a script: doing so could return different text and
# silently invalidate the committed goldens that were baselined against this exact
# entry. It is TRACKED on purpose. See build.mjs's SIMULATOR_CASSETTE doc.
!.generation-cassette/simulator-cassette.json
